{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אשר לא קדמו", :translit "asher lo kidemu", :gloss "who did not come to meet you"} {:he "את הזכרים", :translit "et ha-zechaim", :gloss "with the males"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אשר לא קדמו", :b "את הזכרים"}], :frame {:text "The phrase \"who did not come to meet you\" refers to the Ammonites and Moabites' failure to greet Israel with bread and water (Deuteronomy 23:5). Ba'al HaTurim detects a gematria alluding to a deeper sin: their ambush involved male attackers, evoking the tactic of pinning down specifically the menfolk, as the patriarch Jacob feared when he divided his camp \"male by female\" (Genesis 32:9).", :sources ["Deuteronomy 23:5" "Genesis 32:9"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אשר לא קדמו", :translit "asher lo kidemu", :gloss "who did not meet you"} {:he "אתכם", :translit "etchem", :gloss "you"} {:he "בלק", :translit "balak", :gloss "Balak"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "אתכם", :spells "בלק"} {:kind :gematria, :a "אתכם ר\"ת", :b "בלק"}], :frame {:text "The verse states that Ammon and Moab did not meet Israel with bread and water. While Balaam son of Beor was hired by Balak son of Zippor to curse Israel (Deuteronomy 23:5), the Talmud records that Balak, a Midianite royal, also initiated the plan to seduce Israel into sin at Peor through the daughters of Moab and Midian (Sanhedrin 106a). Ba'al HaTurim's gematria identifies Balak as the hidden instigator behind Moab's hostile failure to provision the Israelites.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 23:5" "Sanhedrin 106a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:a-value 682, :b-value 683, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "את הזכרים", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "אשר לא קדמו"} {:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "אתכם", :spells "בלק", :letters ["א"], :by :selah, :order :mismatch} {:kind :gematria, :a "אתכם ר\"ת", :a-value 1061, :b "בלק", :b-value 132, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23,